1. Causal Reasoning and Origin Metadata
Origin metadata establishes the problem space: The FIMPipeline begins with an origin (the initial causal prompt or input) whose metadata defines the scope and context of the entire problem space. This origin metadata captures the essential problem definition – it delineates what is being addressed and any initial parameters or assumptions. By setting this context, the origin acts as the root of the framework, framing all subsequent analysis (similar to how a problem statement anchors the main branches of a fishbone diagram)​
